From 837fe1d5ebd0092588d6a0be6780a3e3ce182b08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:12:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] antinomie: sample guest memory and root filesystem usage

The host shows how much of the guest's memory and root filesystem is in
use. RESOURCES returns a sample taken in the kernel, so that nothing in
the guest has to read /proc or call statfs for it: MemTotal and
MemAvailable as /proc/meminfo computes them, and statfs of init's root
(total, free, available, the filesystem's device, type and id), each
with its own error.

The command never blocks on a filesystem: it returns the latest
completed sample and its age, and when that is older than 500 ms queues
one refresh, with at most one in flight, so a statfs that hangs leaves
the sample visibly ageing instead of stalling the control channel.

No kernel file outside kernel/antinomie is touched.

Contract: revision 17 (RESOURCES, 0x1070, 96-byte reply).
---
